      "featured_image": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0631/0251/7500/files/image_1_583244eb-e4e0-457c-a08c-256babf23fe6.webp?v=1711728092",
      "description_html": "<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\" data-mce-fragment=\"1\" data-mce-style=\"color: #000000;\">Tom Ford has become one of fashion's great icons. Over the past decade, he has transformed Gucci from a moribund accessories label into one of the sexiest fashion brands in the world. His designs have increased sales at Gucci tenfold and helped build the Gucci brand into the luxury goods conglomerate it is today. <br><br>This book is a complete catalogue of Ford's design work for both Gucci and Yves Saint Laurent from 1994 to 2004. The book not only describes Ford's designs for clothing and accessories for both houses, but also explores Ford's grand vision of the complete design of a brand, including architecture, shop design and advertising. Tom Ford includes more than 200 photographs by Richard Avedon, Mario Testino, Steven Meisel, Helmut Newton, Herb Ritts, Terry Richardson, Craig McDean, Todd Eberle and numerous other photographers, including many never-before-published images.<br><br>Published to mark his departure from Gucci, this book was created with Ford's full cooperation and every page reflects his exceptional taste. It is Ford's testament to a career full of unique moments in which the boundaries of style and sensuality in clothing were reinvented.<br></span></p>\n<p><strong>ISBN</strong><br><span data-mce-fragment=\"1\">9780847826698<br></span><span><strong>PAGES</strong><br>414<br><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'San Francisco', 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 0.875rem;\" class=\"title\"><strong>SIZE</strong><br></span>28,4 × 5,5 × 37,1 cm<br></span></p>"
