      "featured_image": "https://cdn.shopify.com/s/files/1/0631/0251/7500/files/Versace1.jpg?v=1710518005",
      "description_html": "<p><span style=\"color: #000000;\" data-mce-fragment=\"1\" data-mce-style=\"color: #000000;\">Written by Donatella Versace, Maria Luisa Frisa and Stefano Tonchi, Contribution by Tim Blanks and Ingrid Sischy. A long-awaited and highly intimate visual history of Versace, the glamorous and globally renowned Italian fashion house. Versace—a name that epitomizes Italian opulence, bold sexiness, and a flair for the extravagant—holds its place firmly in the fashion world as a legendary and iconic luxury brand. Taking over the creative artistic direction of the family-run fashion house in 1997, the enigmatic and alluring Donatella Versace has since catapulted the brand into popular culture, cementing Versace as a go-to label for A-list celebrities. This richly illustrated tome chronicles Donatella’s interpretation of Versace in the twenty-first century and her remarkable work as the curator and face of Versace.<br></span></p>\n<p><strong>ISBN</strong><br><span data-mce-fragment=\"1\">9780847846078<br></span><span><strong>PAGES</strong><br>336<br><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, 'San Francisco', 'Segoe UI', Roboto, 'Helvetica Neue', sans-serif; font-size: 0.875rem;\" class=\"title\"><strong>SIZE</strong><br></span>28,5 x 35,3 x 3,1 cm<br></span></p>"
